{#-
Abstracted scene context for autonomous scene direction.

Replaces verbatim scene dialogue with summaries, world state and character
notes. Used when `director.scene_direction.abstract_context` is on, so the
director can run on a censored or remote model without the scene's prose being
sent to it.

Deliberately does not reach for the scene's message history at all — the normal
context helper mixes summaries with verbatim dialogue by design. Everything here
is drawn from already-summarised material, so no dialogue can leak through this
path. A test enforces that this file never references that helper.

Expects: `budget` (tokens available for this section).
-#}
{% set summary_entries = [] %}
{#- Most abstract first: the highest layer is the broadest arc summary. -#}
{% for layer in scene.layered_history|reverse %}
{% for entry in layer %}
{% if entry.get("text") %}{% set _ = summary_entries.append(entry["text"]) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{#- Then the per-chunk archive summaries, oldest to newest. -#}
{% for entry in scene.archived_history %}
{% if entry.get("text") %}{% set _ = summary_entries.append(entry["text"]) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{#- Trim from the front so the most recent summaries survive the budget. -#}
{% set kept = [] %}
{% set used = [0] %}
{% for text in summary_entries|reverse %}
{% set cost = count_tokens(text) %}
{% if used[0] + cost <= budget %}
{% set _ = kept.append(text) %}
{% set _ = used.__setitem__(0, used[0] + cost) %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<|SECTION:STORY SO FAR|>
{% if kept %}
Summarised account of what has happened, oldest first. The exact wording of recent dialogue is deliberately withheld — direct from these summaries and the current state below.

{% for text in kept|reverse %}
- {{ text|condensed }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
Nothing has been summarised yet. The scene is either new or too short to have produced summaries, so judge from the current state below and the scene intent.
{% endif %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>

{% set ws = scene.world_state %}
{% set state_body %}
{%- if ws.location %}Location: {{ ws.location|condensed }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if ws.characters.values()|selectattr("snapshot")|list %}
### Characters
{% for name, char in ws.characters.items() if char.snapshot %}- {{ name }}{% if char.emotion %} ({{ char.emotion }}){% endif %} — {{ char.snapshot|condensed }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
{%- if ws.items.values()|selectattr("snapshot")|list %}
### Items
{% for name, item in ws.items.items() if item.snapshot %}- {{ name }} — {{ item.snapshot|condensed }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
{%- if ws.places.values()|selectattr("snapshot")|list %}
### Places
{% for name, place in ws.places.items() if place.snapshot %}- {{ name }} — {{ place.snapshot|condensed }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
{% endset %}
{% if state_body|trim %}
<|SECTION:CURRENT STATE|>
What is true right now.

{{ state_body|trim }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif %}

{% set active_body %}
{%- for character in scene.characters %}
- {{ character.name }}{% if character.is_player %} (the user's character){% endif %}{% if character.description %} — {{ character.description|condensed }}{% endif %}
{% endfor -%}
{% endset %}
{% if active_body|trim %}
<|SECTION:CHARACTERS IN THE SCENE|>
{{ active_body|trim }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif %}

<|SECTION:IMPORTANT NOTES|>
STORY TITLE: {{ scene.title or scene.name or "<None>" }}
ABSTRACTED CONTEXT: You are directing from summaries, not from the scene text. Do not attempt to quote or continue exact wording; give instructions describing what should happen, and let the actors and narrator write it.
{% if not scene.num_history_entries %}
UNPLAYED: There has been no progress in the interactive story yet.
{% endif %}
{% if not scene.context %}
CONTENT CLASSIFICATION MISSING: The content classification is missing.
{% endif %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
